l)	NSAG information;

m)	RAN timing synchronization.

o)	S-NSSAI location validity information;

p)	Discontinuous coverage maximum time offset; and

q)	access technology utilization control information.

The following parameters are managed and sent per access type i.e. independently over 3GPP access or non-3GPP access:

a)	Allowed NSSAI;

b)	Rejected NSSAI (when the NSSAI is rejected for the current registration area or is rejected for the maximum number of UEs reached); and

c)	If the UE is not registered to the same PLMN or SNPN over 3GPP and non-3GPP access:

-	5G-GUTI;

-	NITZ information;

-	Rejected NSSAI (when the NSSAI is rejected for the current PLMN or SNPN or rejected for the failed or revoked NSSAA);

